  designNotes: "2026-08-27, explicit user request (\u5C0E\u5165 Meshy_AI_Parkside_Portrait_biped
    (9).zip \u4F5C\u70BA\u5B9A\u6642\u5C0F\u6280\u80FD\uFF0C\u6230\u9B25\u6BCF\u7D93\u904E20\u79D2\u5C31\u89F8\u767C\uFF0C\u5148\u98DB\u5347\u5230\u7A7A\u4E2D\uFF0C\u7136\u5F8C\u843D\u5730\u5287\u780D\uFF0C\u843D\u5730\u6642\u9396\u5B9A\u73A9\u5BB6\uFF0C\u843D\u4E0B\u671F\u9593\u5168\u7A0B\u6709\u653B\u64CA\u5E40\u3001\u7BC4\u570D\u5927)
    - measured via AnimationMode.SampleAnimationClip against the live Wushi character
    (whole 3.03s clip, tracking Hips-bone world Y and BladeHitbox speed relative
    to root every ~0.017s). Confirmed the clip's rise-and-fall is ENTIRELY baked
    into the Hips bone's own local animation - root Transform position never moves
    at all during the whole clip (measured 0.000 drift throughout) - so \"landing
    on the player\" is achieved by teleporting Wushi's root to the player's current
    XZ position (own grounded Y kept) and committing facing ONCE in TryEnterLeapSlam
    right before this state starts, not by tracking mid-air. Motion profile: crouch/wind-up
    t=0-0.13, RISE t=0.13-0.32 (Hips climbs from ~2 up to a peak of ~11 units, i.e.
    real airborne height given Wushi's 4x scale), FALL t=0.32-0.53 (Hips drops from
    11 back to ~1.8, blade speed peaks at a violent 108.3 units/s at t=0.533 - the
    actual slam impact, faster than any other measured attack in this project), held
    landing pose t=0.55-0.80, stand back up t=0.80-1.0. Hit window (0.32-0.56) deliberately
    covers the WHOLE fall through to just after impact settles, not just the landing
    instant, per the explicit \"\u5168\u7A0B\u5177\u6709\u653B\u64CA\u5E40\" request.
    Uses the existing LandingAOE hitbox slot (part 5) - a purpose-built large SphereCollider
    (world radius 3.0, several times any normal attack's reach) newly wired to Wushi
    specifically for this move, matching the explicit \"\u7BC4\u570D\u5927\" request;
    that slot/field already existed in the architecture for the (currently-disabled)
    Vanish/DiveAttack cycle but was never actually used by Wushi until now. Never
    part of normalAttackPool - selectionWeight/maxDistance/maxAngle/cooldown are
    all irrelevant leftovers from the shared BossAttackDefinition schema (queued
    purely by BossTuning.LeapSlamTriggerSeconds combat-time timer instead, see TryEnterLeapSlam)
    - maxDistance/maxAngle set to effectively unlimited and cooldownSeconds to 0
    so they can never accidentally gate anything if this ever gets referenced from
    a distance/angle-aware path by mistake. interruptible=0 + superArmorDuringActiveWindows=1
    since a boss committed to an aerial slam shouldn't be punch-stopped mid-leap.\n\n2026-08-27
    follow-up, explicit user request (\"\u4E0D\u80FD\u8DF3\u5F88\u9AD8\u55CE \u81F3\u5C11\u8B93\u73A9\u5BB6\u770B\u4E0D\u5230\u7684\u9AD8\u5EA6
    \u5F9E\u4E0A\u800C\u4E0B\u5288\u780D \u50B7\u5BB3500\") - the clip's own baked
    ~11-unit rise wasn't remotely \"off-screen\", so BossStateMachine.UpdateLeapSlam
    now layers an EXTRA script-driven height arc on top of it via BossTuning.LeapSlamExtraHeight
    (default 30 world units, ~41 combined with the clip's own motion) - driven through
    _verticalVelocity every frame, not the animation itself, so it's tunable without
    re-editing the clip. Damage raised to 500 (poise to 60 to match the escalated
    severity) - at the player's established 500 max HP this is a genuine one-shot-if-you-
    don't-move punish, which is the intended trade for how dramatically telegraphed
    (character vanishes upward) and wide (3.0 world-unit radius) the warning is."
